  {
   "slug": "about",
   "title": "About",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We are a small team of players who write about games the way we talk about them with friends: honestly, with plenty of enthusiasm and no hype for hype's sake.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How we score</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>9 and up</strong>: a must-play, the kind of game you recommend to everyone.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>7 to 8.9</strong>: great, with flaws worth knowing about.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>5 to 6.9</strong>: for fans of the genre.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Below 5</strong>: we would rather you spent the evening on something else.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We buy most of the games we review. When a studio sends a copy, the review says so, and it never changes the score.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:controller-glow}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:controller-glow}}\" alt=\"A game controller outlined in neon light\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:controller-glow}}\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image -->",
   "featured_media": "arcade-cabinets"
  },
  {
   "slug": "review-policy",
   "title": "Review Policy",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Every review is written after finishing the main story or playing at least fifteen hours, whichever comes first.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Scores are decided by the reviewer and checked by one editor. We do not accept payment for coverage, and advertisers never see reviews before they are published.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>If a game changes a lot after launch, we add an update note at the top of the review rather than quietly changing the score.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "parent": "about"
  },
  {
   "slug": "contact",
   "title": "Contact",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Got a tip, a correction or a game we should play? We read everything.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:columns --><div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Tips &amp; news</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>tips@pixelarcade.example</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Studios &amp; review copies</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>press@pixelarcade.example</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Newsletter</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Reply to any newsletter to talk to a human.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:column --></div><!-- /wp:columns --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We answer most messages within two working days.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->"
  }
 ],
 "posts": [
  {
   "slug": "starfall-drift-review",
   "title": "Starfall Drift review: a quiet space opera that earns every jump",
   "date": "2026-10-24T10:00:00",
   "excerpt": "A small studio's debut turns cargo runs between dying moons into the most moving space game of the year.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Starfall Drift opens with a cargo manifest and a broken heater, and somehow that is enough. You fly a patched-up hauler between the moons of a planet that is slowly losing its rings, and every delivery is a small story: a crate of seeds for a greenhouse colony, a letter for a lighthouse keeper who has not had a visitor in years.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The flying is weighty without being fussy. Thrusters stutter when you overload the hold, and the ring debris drifts in patterns you learn to read like weather. By the third evening I was planning routes the way you plan a walk home, choosing the scenic lane over the fast one.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Built for long evenings</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>There is no combat, and the game never pretends there should be. Tension comes from fuel, from time and from the radio, which picks up fragments of other pilots who are clearly having worse days than you.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:synth-sunset}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:synth-sunset}}\" alt=\"A striped synthwave sun setting behind pixel mountains\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:synth-sunset}}\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Sunset over the outer moons, seen from the cockpit.</figcaption></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:quote --><blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>It is the rare game that makes doing your job feel like a kindness.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><cite>Our review notes</cite></blockquote><!-- /wp:quote --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Its last act stumbles a little, with one too many fetch loops before the finale, but the ending lands softly and stays with you. Bring headphones; the soundtrack does half of the storytelling.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"pa-verdict\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group pa-verdict\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"pa-score\"} --><p class=\"pa-score\">9.1</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The verdict</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"pa-verdict__line\"} --><p class=\"pa-verdict__line\">A gentle, gorgeous haul across a dying sky. One of the year's best.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:columns --><div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"pa-pros\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group pa-pros\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":4} --><h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Power-ups</h4><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Weighty, readable flight model</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Radio chatter that builds a world</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>A soundtrack worth buying</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"pa-cons\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group pa-cons\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":4} --><h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Glitches</h4><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Late-game fetch loops</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Map screen is cramped</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:column --></div><!-- /wp:columns --></div><!-- /wp:group -->",
   "categories": [
    "reviews"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "pc",
    "console",
    "indie"
   ],
   "featured_media": "starfall-drift",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": true,
   "comments": [
    {
     "author": "Rook Calder",
     "content": "Played it in two sittings. The lighthouse delivery broke me.",
     "date": "2026-10-24T18:20:00",
     "email": "rook@example.com"
    },
    {
     "author": "Mina Torres",
     "content": "Agree about the map screen. Hoping for a patch.",
     "date": "2026-10-25T09:05:00",
     "email": "mina@example.com"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "slug": "moss-and-iron-review",
   "title": "Moss & Iron review: a soulful knight in a forest that remembers",
   "date": "2026-10-20T09:00:00",
   "excerpt": "A hand-drawn action adventure with punishing bosses, generous checkpoints and a forest full of ghosts.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Moss & Iron wants you to die, and then it wants you to come back a little wiser. You play a knight whose armour is rusting faster than she can fight, and each boss you topple feeds the forest that is slowly swallowing the old kingdom.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Combat is all about stamina. Swing too often and your knight stumbles; parry on the beat and she glides. It clicks around the second boss, a hollow stag that fills the arena with falling leaves.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Checkpoints that respect your time</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Shrines are placed right before every boss door.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Lost gear waits where you fell, marked by a glowing mushroom.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>A difficulty assist slows enemies without changing patterns.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:boss-fight}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:boss-fight}}\" alt=\"A giant pixel dragon facing a tiny hero on a bridge\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:boss-fight}}\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">The bridge duel is the highlight of the second act.</figcaption></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Its pixel art is extraordinary: moss creeps across the screen as you play, and areas you have cleared look greener when you return. It is a small touch, and it makes the map feel alive.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"pa-verdict\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group pa-verdict\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"pa-score\"} --><p class=\"pa-score\">8.7</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The verdict</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"pa-verdict__line\"} --><p class=\"pa-verdict__line\">Hard, fair and full of heart. A forest you will want to get lost in.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:columns --><div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"pa-pros\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group pa-pros\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":4} --><h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Power-ups</h4><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Tight stamina-based combat</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Living, changing pixel art</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Smart assist options</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"pa-cons\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group pa-cons\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":4} --><h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Glitches</h4><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Two bosses reuse attacks</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Some backtracking</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:column --></div><!-- /wp:columns --></div><!-- /wp:group -->",
   "categories": [
    "reviews"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "console",
    "handheld",
