  {
   "slug": "lantern-keep-preview",
   "title": "Hands-on: Lantern Keep turns castle defence into a cosy puzzle",
   "date": "2026-10-11T12:00:00",
   "excerpt": "We played two hours of the upcoming strategy game where every lantern you light changes how the night attacks.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>In Lantern Keep the night is the enemy, and light is your only wall. You place lanterns around a hilltop castle, and every lantern you light changes which paths the shadows can take.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We played the first two hours of the campaign. The early nights are gentle, but by the fourth the shadows start splitting around your light, and you find yourself rearranging the whole keep at dusk.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What we liked</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Every level fits on one screen, no scrolling</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Undo is unlimited during the day</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>A calm soundtrack that grows as the night deepens</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:pullquote --><figure class=\"wp-block-pullquote\"><blockquote><p>It is a tower defence game that feels like tidying a room before guests arrive.</p></blockquote></figure><!-- /wp:pullquote --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Lantern Keep is due early next year, and a demo is planned for the winter showcase.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "previews"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "pc",
    "indie"
   ],
   "featured_media": "lantern-keep",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false
  },
  {
   "slug": "winter-showcase-roundup",
   "title": "Winter Indie Showcase: the twelve games we can't stop thinking about",
   "date": "2026-10-06T18:00:00",
   "excerpt": "From a cooking game set on a submarine to a rhythm brawler, the showcase was stacked. Here are our picks.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>This year's winter showcase ran for ninety minutes and did not waste one of them. There were no live-service pitches and no shareholder slides, just small teams showing the games they have been quietly building.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Our shortlist</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} --><ol class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Galley Below</strong>: cook for a submarine crew as the pressure rises.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Beat Brawl</strong>: a fighting game where every punch lands on the beat.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Paper Comet</strong>: fold your ship to change how it flies.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Night Market Tycoon</strong>: run a food stall from dusk to dawn.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Lantern Keep</strong>: our hands-on is already up.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ol><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:controller-glow}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:controller-glow}}\" alt=\"A game controller outlined in neon light\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:controller-glow}}\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Most showcase demos support any controller.</figcaption></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Most of these have demos available today, and several land before the end of the year. We will be covering the best of them in full.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:quote --><blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Small teams, big ideas, zero trailers that were just logos.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><cite>Our showcase chat</cite></blockquote><!-- /wp:quote -->",
   "categories": [
    "news"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "indie",
