  {
   "slug": "retro-handheld-buyers-guide",
   "title": "The retro handheld buyer's guide: what to look for in 2026",
   "date": "2026-09-29T09:30:00",
   "excerpt": "Screens, sticks, battery and build: a no-nonsense checklist before you buy a pocket console for old favourites.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Pocket consoles built for classic games have never been better or more confusing. Dozens of models, all with similar names and very different screens. Here is what actually matters.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The checklist</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:table {\"className\":\"pa-release-table\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-table pa-release-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>What to look for</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Screen</td><td>4:3 for older consoles, 16:9 for later ones</td></tr><tr><td>Brightness</td><td>At least 400 nits for outdoor play</td></tr><tr><td>Controls</td><td>Clicky face buttons, a real d-pad</td></tr><tr><td>Battery</td><td>Five hours of play at medium brightness</td></tr><tr><td>Storage</td><td>A card slot you can reach without a screwdriver</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><!-- /wp:table --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Above all, buy for the games you actually want to play. A pocket device that is perfect for 8-bit platformers can struggle with 3D games, and that is fine.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:cartridge-shelf}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:cartridge-shelf}}\" alt=\"A shelf of colourful retro game cartridges\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:cartridge-shelf}}\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Your old cartridges deserve a good screen.</figcaption></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Only play games you own, and back up your saves. The most common complaint we hear is a lost save file, not a bad screen.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "guides",
    "hardware"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "handheld",
    "retro"
   ],
   "featured_media": "handheld-console",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false
  },
  {
   "slug": "speedrun-marathon-recap",
   "title": "Speedrun marathon recap: records, raffles and one very fast frog",
   "date": "2026-09-22T20:00:00",
   "excerpt": "A week of runs raised money for a children's hospital and produced three new world records. Here are the highlights.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The autumn speedrun marathon wrapped on Sunday after seven days of runs, raffles and remarkably calm commentary. The final total went to a children's hospital charity, and the chat stayed kind from the first run to the last.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Three records</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>A frog platformer finished in 11 minutes 42 seconds, with a skip nobody had seen before.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>A racing game cup cleared without a single drift.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>A puzzle classic solved blindfolded, with the runner reading the music.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:handheld-console}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:handheld-console}}\" alt=\"A pixel handheld console with a green screen\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:handheld-console}}\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">A few runners played on pocket consoles.</figcaption></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Between runs, the volunteers raffled off a hand-built arcade stick and a stack of signed posters from the studios whose games were on the schedule. The stick went to a viewer who had donated every single night.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The organisers say next spring's event will add a beginners' block, where newer runners show categories they are still learning.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "news",
    "esports"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "community",
    "retro"
   ],
   "featured_media": "speedrun-timer",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false
  },
  {
   "slug": "vr-comfort-settings",
   "title": "Every VR comfort setting explained, and which ones to turn on",
   "date": "2026-09-15T11:15:00",
   "excerpt": "Vignettes, snap turning and seated modes: a plain-language guide to staying comfortable in virtual reality.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Feeling queasy in VR is common and nothing to be embarrassed about. The good news is that most games now include settings that help, and they work better than you might expect.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Start with these</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Snap turning</strong>: turn in steps instead of smoothly.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Vignette</strong>: darkens the edges of your view while you move.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Teleport movement</strong>: jump to a point instead of walking.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Seated mode</strong>: lowers the camera so you can play sitting down.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Turn them on first, play in short sessions, and switch them off one at a time as you get comfortable. Fresh air and a fan pointed at you help more than you would think.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:quote --><blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Comfort settings are not training wheels. They are just settings.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><cite>A developer we spoke to</cite></blockquote><!-- /wp:quote -->",
   "categories": [
    "guides"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "vr",
    "pc"
   ],
   "featured_media": "vr-grid",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false
  },
  {
   "slug": "arcade-revival",
   "title": "The arcade is back: inside the bars reviving cabinets downtown",
   "date": "2026-09-08T16:45:00",
   "excerpt": "Neon, tokens and a waiting list for the rhythm machines. We spent a Friday night in the new arcade scene.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>On a Friday night the queue outside the arcade on Wharf Street stretches past the bakery next door. Inside, forty cabinets hum in the dark, and the rhythm machines have a paper waiting list.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The owners restore every cabinet themselves. Monitors are rebuilt, buttons replaced, and the cabinets that cannot be saved become parts for the ones that can.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:cartridge-shelf}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:cartridge-shelf}}\" alt=\"A shelf of colourful retro game cartridges\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:cartridge-shelf}}\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">The back room keeps spare boards and cartridges.</figcaption></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why now?</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Regulars give the same answer: it is the one place where playing a game is something you do with strangers in the room. High scores are written on a chalkboard, and the best players teach newcomers between rounds.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:gallery {\"columns\":3,\"linkTo\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-3 is-cropped\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:controller-glow}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:controller-glow}}\" alt=\"A game controller outlined in neon light\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:controller-glow}}\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:handheld-console}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:handheld-console}}\" alt=\"A pixel handheld console with a green screen\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:handheld-console}}\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:synth-sunset}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:synth-sunset}}\" alt=\"A striped synthwave sun setting behind pixel mountains\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:synth-sunset}}\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --></figure><!-- /wp:gallery -->",
   "categories": [
    "features"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "retro",
    "community"
   ],
   "featured_media": "arcade-cabinets",
